source/reference_guide/transforms.rst:97: (Normalised) ["Normalized"] Normalised 3-vector
source/reference_guide/transforms.rst:226: (neighbour) ["neighbor"] Maximum stencil size (nearest-neighbour count), an alternative to 
source/reference_guide/transforms.rst:246: (morpher) ["morphed", "morph er", "morph-er", "morpheme", "perimorph", "morph"]  only). Unlike the other IDW fields above, the C++ morpher reads this value unconditionally with no fallback, so it should always be given explicitly for an 
source/reference_guide/transforms.rst:259: (optimisation) ["optimization", "improvisation", "misapplication", "misappropriation", "imitation"]  flag, restricting each partition’s RBF solve to only the nodes it owns (a memory/performance optimisation for large parallel RBF problems). It is not part of the schema: no control deck sets it, every live RBF/IDW test case runs correctly using the full node set, and the C++ read is guarded (defaults to using all nodes when the key is absent), so leaving it unset changes nothing for any existing deck.
